Cruis'n USA (Midway V-Unit, midvunit.cpp) at the arcade bar: driven from the bar's keys.

- Controls, as the bar's Daytona USA: the fork's per-game button profile (mame_buttons_profiles,
  input_retro.cpp's Input_Binding) for crusnusa and its clones sets retro_driving, and the
  RetroPad's d-pad drives: Left/Right are the wheel's decrement/increment (IPT_PADDLE), as MAME's
  arrow keys are on a keyboard, so the wheel turns at the field's key delta per frame and comes
  back to the middle when let go; Up presses the gas pedal (IPT_PEDAL) and Down the brake
  (IPT_PEDAL2) the same way. The fork's own button pedals (Button 1/2's switches) are left out for
  it: Button 1 is the radio. Buttons: B/A shift down/up (Button 5/6), Y X L the views 1-3 (Button
  2-4), R the radio (Button 1). patches/0002 names them all on the input descriptors.
- midvunit.cpp: the shifter is "Sequential" by default (it was "Buttons (sticky)", a button per
  gear and one for neutral): Shift Up from neutral is 1st gear, then 2nd, 3rd, 4th; Shift Down
  back to neutral. The driver's own setting, for spring-return shifters, paddles or buttons; the
  shifter's position is in the driver's save state.
- tms320c3x.cpp: the TMS320C31's internal boot loader ROM (c31boot.bin, "assembled from
  c31boot.asm", MAME's tms320c31 device set) is optional, zeros when missing. Only the CPU's
  microcomputer/boot loader mode maps it, which Midway V-Unit never selects (its C31 boots from
  the game's ROMs), and the game's set doesn't have it: MAME refused to start without it.

diff --git a/src/devices/cpu/tms320c3x/tms320c3x.cpp b/src/devices/cpu/tms320c3x/tms320c3x.cpp
index 87adeea1..a7e0e12a 100644
--- a/src/devices/cpu/tms320c3x/tms320c3x.cpp
+++ b/src/devices/cpu/tms320c3x/tms320c3x.cpp
@@ -263,9 +263,12 @@ ROM_START( tms320c30 )
 	ROM_LOAD( "c30boot.bin", 0x0000, 0x4000, BAD_DUMP CRC(bddc2763) SHA1(96b2170ecee5bec5abaa1741bb2d3b6096ecc262)) // TODO: programmable?
 ROM_END
 
+// The arcade bar: optional (zeros when missing). Only microcomputer/boot loader mode maps it, which
+// no driver in the bar's core uses (Midway V-Unit's C31 boots from its own ROMs, MCBL/MP low),
+// and the game sets there don't carry this device set (tms320c31.zip).
 ROM_START( tms320c31 )
-	ROM_REGION(0x4000, "internal_rom", 0)
-	ROM_LOAD( "c31boot.bin", 0x0000, 0x4000, BAD_DUMP CRC(bddc2763) SHA1(96b2170ecee5bec5abaa1741bb2d3b6096ecc262) ) // Assembled from c31boot.asm (02-07-92)
+	ROM_REGION(0x4000, "internal_rom", ROMREGION_ERASE00)
+	ROM_LOAD_OPTIONAL( "c31boot.bin", 0x0000, 0x4000, BAD_DUMP CRC(bddc2763) SHA1(96b2170ecee5bec5abaa1741bb2d3b6096ecc262) ) // Assembled from c31boot.asm (02-07-92)
 ROM_END
 
 ROM_START( tms320c32 )
